<http://data.silknow.org/object/715a9e91-8f74-33a8-b3c0-8ceb57190bca/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Panel of silk which has a white ground with a zig-zag meander of fruit and flowers.\nThe pattern is brocaded in coloured silks with alternative comber repeats of blue and pink flowers and fruit. The colouring is subdued; the blue repeat having dark green leaves shaded in black, whereas the pink repeat has soft olive green leaves highlighted with a pale, creamy green. The white ground is woven in tabby with an additional warp forming a flush chevron pattern.\nThe panel retains the left selvedge,  which is narrow, self-coloured and has seven cords.\nThis piece has been sewn as a panel between an orange damask silk, the seams of which remain."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/715a9e91-8f74-33a8-b3c0-8ceb57190bca> .

