        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Silk panel, France, 1730-1765."@en , "Panel of silk which has a white ground with a zig-zag meander of fruit and flowers.\nThe pattern is brocaded in coloured silks with alternative comber repeats of blue and pink flowers and fruit. The colouring is subdued; the blue repeat having dark green leaves shaded in black, whereas the pink repeat has soft olive green leaves highlighted with a pale, creamy green. The white ground is woven in tabby with an additional warp forming a flush chevron pattern.\nThe panel retains the left selvedge,  which is narrow, self-coloured and has seven cords.\nThis piece has been sewn as a panel between an orange damask silk, the seams of which remain."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/adf87191-a3d6-30e6-84c3-5909324a0ac9> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Panel of silk which has a white ground with a zig-zag meander of fruit and flowers.\nThe pattern is brocaded in coloured silks with alternative comber repeats of blue and pink flowers and fruit. The colouring is subdued; the blue repeat having dark green leaves shaded in black, whereas the pink repeat has soft olive green leaves highlighted with a pale, creamy green. The white ground is woven in tabby with an additional warp forming a flush chevron pattern.\nThe panel retains the left selvedge,  which is narrow, self-coloured and has seven cords.\nThis piece has been sewn as a panel between an orange damask silk, the seams of which remain."@en , "Silk panel, France, 1730-1765."@en ;
